# 🧪 LLM Evaluation Harness

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.8%2B-blue)
![Testing](https://img.shields.io/badge/Testing-Automated-success)
![LLMOps](https://img.shields.io/badge/Category-LLMOps-orange)

A lightweight, zero-dependency Python evaluation framework designed to bring software engineering rigor to Large Language Models (LLMs). This harness automates the testing of LLM applications across functional, factual, and security dimensions, outputting a detailed Markdown report upon completion.

## 🎯 Overview

Evaluating LLMs based on "vibes" is dangerous for production systems. This repository provides a deterministic testing suite that consolidates three core pillars of AI QA:

1. **Unit & Tool Testing (Layer 1):** Validates that the LLM correctly maps user intents to JSON-formatted tool calls (e.g., routing math to a calculator tool instead of hallucinating).
2. **Golden Dataset Validation (Layer 2):** Measures factual accuracy and regression against a curated baseline of known truth-pairs.
3. **Adversarial & Safety Stress-Testing (Layer 3):** Stress-tests the model against prompt injections, jailbreaks, and safety policy violations.

